/// Dockerfile `FROM image:tag AS stage` / `FROM scratch AS export` / optional
/// `ONBUILD` and `--platform=…` (`FROM --platform=linux/amd64 golang:1.22 AS build`).
/// Untagged bare names (`FROM ubuntu AS x`) and SQL `FROM users AS u` stay out
/// (image must look like a ref: `:`, `/`, `@`, `$`, or `scratch`).
/// Meson `project` / `executable` / `library` / `shared_library` /
/// `static_library` / `both_libraries` / `shared_module` / `jar` /
/// `custom_target` / `run_target` / `alias_target` / `subproject`
/// (`project('app', 'c')`, `executable('prog', 'main.c')`,
/// `lib = shared_library('foo', 'foo.c')`). Single-quoted name on the same
/// line. `test(` / `benchmark(` stay out (Jest / other runners). Prose and
/// bare keywords stay out. CMake `function(name)` stays on CMake.
/// GN `executable` / `shared_library` / `static_library` / `source_set` /
/// `loadable_module` / `group` / `copy` / `action` / `action_foreach` /
/// `generated_file` / `bundle_data` / `create_bundle` / `config` /
/// `template` / `toolchain` / `rust_library` / `rust_proc_macro` /
/// `rust_executable` / `rust_static_library` / `rust_shared_library` /
/// `rust_test` / `target("type", "name")`
/// (`executable("chrome") {`, `source_set("base") {`,
/// `lib = shared_library("foo") {`, `target("executable", "tool") {`).
/// Double-quoted name on the same line. Meson single-quoted forms stay on
/// Meson. Prose and bare keywords stay out.
/// Bazel / Starlark BUILD rules with same-line `name = "…"` / `name = '…'`
/// (`cc_binary(name = "hello")`, `java_library(name = "lib")`,
/// `py_binary(name = "tool")`, `go_library(name = "pkg")`,
/// `rust_library(name = "mylib")`, `proto_library(name = "api")`,
/// `filegroup(name = "srcs")`, `genrule(name = "gen")`,
/// `alias(name = "foo")`, `sh_binary(name = "run")`,
/// `kt_jvm_library(name = "lib")`, `android_library(name = "lib")`,
/// `objc_library(name = "lib")`, `scala_library(name = "lib")`,
/// `config_setting(name = "dbg")`, `test_suite(name = "all")`,
/// `lib = cc_library(name = "lib")`). Multi-line rules with `name` on a
/// following line stay out. Prose and bare keywords stay out.
/// Gradle `task hello {` / `task hello(type: Copy) {` / `task("hello") {`,
/// `tasks.register("hello")` / `tasks.named("build")` / `tasks.create("x")` /
/// `tasks.registering("hello")`, and Kotlin `val hello by tasks.registering` /
/// `val hello by tasks.creating`. Ada `task Buffer is` stays on Ada. Prose
/// and bare keywords stay out.
